pcbkit 2

// ESP32-C6-MINI-1-N4 (Espressif Systems): Small Wi-Fi 6 (802.11ax), Bluetooth LE 5 and 802.15.4
// (Thread, Zigbee) module, single-core RISC-V 160 MHz (ESP32-C6), 4 MB flash, USB Serial/JTAG, PCB
// antenna, 3.3 V
// Compiled from the part sheet `parts/ESP32_C6_MINI_1.json` (`parts.create`); status: checked.
// Datasheet:
// https://www.espressif.com/sites/default/files/documentation/esp32-c6-mini-1_mini-1u_datasheet_en.pdf
// (v1.5)
// Pins: Espressif ESP32-C6-MINI-1 & MINI-1U datasheet v1.5, Table 3-1 Pin Definitions and Figure
// 3-1 Pin Layout; land pattern from Figures 10-1 and 11-1 (identical to ESP32-C3-MINI-1)
// Footprint: the datasheet's land pattern
// This file may be used, changed and shared without conditions, with the board or alone.

// Note: Supply: 3.0-3.6 V able to deliver 500 mA; 22 uF and 100 nF at the 3V3 pin.
// Note: Strapping pins sampled at reset: IO9 (weak pull-up; low = download mode, the BOOT button),
// IO8 (floating; must be high for download mode: 10 kohm pull-up), IO4/IO5 (SDIO edges, floating),
// IO15 (JTAG source, read only when an eFuse enables it). Do not load them with circuits that pull
// the wrong way during reset.
// Note: Every GPIO reaches UART, SPI, I2C, I2S, LEDC PWM, MCPWM, PCNT, TWAI (CAN; needs an
// external transceiver) and RMT through the GPIO matrix; ADC1 on IO0-IO6; LP I2C on IO6/IO7, LP
// UART on IO4/IO5.
// Note: Pins 36-53 and 1, 2, 11, 14 are ground pads: connect them all; NC pads stay unconnected.
// Note: Antenna: the antenna area is the top 5.4 mm of the module (the edge with ground pads
// 36-48). The footprint keeps tracks, vias, pours and other parts out of the antenna area itself
// (the module's width plus 0.5 mm, and 0.5 mm beyond its edge), the minimum the datasheet marks as
// the keepout zone. The vendor's hardware design guidelines (Positioning a Module on a Base Board)
// strongly recommend the antenna outside the base board, or its feed point at the board edge with
// the board cut away beside and below it, and at least 15 mm of clearance around it in the
// product: place the module at a board edge with the antenna overhanging it (`place = [edge(.top,
// overhang = 5.4mm)]`: the rule's `overhang` is a Length, how far beyond the edge), keep copper
// and parts as far from the antenna as the board allows, and put ground copper with dense ground
// vias on the board near (not under) the antenna.

